{
	title: 'SYSTEM.md: the Hal prompt lives in a file',
	description: "Hal's own system prompt text lives in SYSTEM.md at the root of the hal2 checkout, not in code: the one-line identity becomes the start of that file. systemPrompt.build reads it as one of its inputs (like the AGENTS.md chain), so the prompt stays byte-identical between requests while the file is unchanged, and an edited SYSTEM.md takes effect on the next request without a restart. The file starts minimal: who Hal is, and a few rules from the old one (tasks/29/old-SYSTEM.md) that hold for hal2 today (tools it really has; no eval, spawn or IPC text until those exist). It grows by the user's edits, not by agents inventing policy. The OAuth identity-block rules of task 29 still hold (blank line before our block).",
	status: 'planned',
	needs: ['29'],
	foldInto: ['29']
}
